  "prompt_mode": "chat_continuation",
  "prompt_text": "Continue the given text:\nWhen you're 28, science discovers a drug that stops all effects of aging, creating immortality. Your government decides to give the drug to all citizens under 26, but you and the rest of the \"Lost Generations\" are deemed too high-risk. When you're 85, the side effects are finally discovered.\n\n\n\nThis is the story of a group of people who are forced to live with the consequences of immortality. The negative being that although you are not aging and are technically immortal, you are also not given the positive effects of aging. For example, you do not become any more wise, you do not learn from your mistakes, and you are not able to become a better person. Essentially, people are stuck exactly where they were when they received the drug. This turns people mad in a way, forced into lives of repetitiveness. The suicide rates go up, murder rates go up, and violence in general. Although people are not dying from old age, they are now dying more often from homicide.",
  "reference_single_token_nfa_states": 33,
  "reference_text": " The world is much more dangerous than it was pre-immortality drug. Since the immortal have stopped the side effects of aging, when they have kids the kids remain kids. Therefore, if the immortal race is wiped out there will be nothing but babies left on the planet. This will cause humans to die out completely.",
